<title>UK: Deutsche Finance adds 1.0 trln to zero coupon bond.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Finance adds 1.0 trln to zero coupon bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond announced by lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell has been increased by 1.0 trillion lire to 3.0 trillion lire.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE FINANCE NETHERLANDS</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  DEUTSCHE BANK</p>
<p> AMT   *3.0 TRLN LIRE COUPON     ZERO	MATURITY    20.JAN.32</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE**8.35	PAY DATE    20.JAN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.25	REOFFER  **8.225     SPREAD	 =</p>
<p> MOODY	=	   LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  =	   DENOMS (M) 5-50-500  SALE LIMS US/UK/NL/IT</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.125     SELL CONC  0.125     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p> NOTES     *ORIGINALLY LAUNCHED FOR 2.0 TRILLION ON 07.JAN.97</p>
<p>	    **NEW ISSUE AND REOFFER PRICE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
